1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
Welcome to Tile Glider and the XPlanar Experiment Configurator—an end-to-end platform for flexible planar manufacturing.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,500
Creating a new experiment is modular and intuitive. We begin by naming our trial and assembling our preconfigured building blocks.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,500
First, we select an existing solver configuration—choosing a high-throughput CPLEX model with twelve movers.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Next, we select our factory layout. The digital twin renders immediately; hovering reagents dynamically illuminates their physical dispensers.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Finally, we attach our preloaded recipe order set and submit the experiment to solve in the background.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
While our new trial is solving, let's inspect a completed run below it. The Details view exposes full solver parameters and factory twin allocations.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,000
We can review recipe sequences, inspect live Gantt milestones, and validate the embedded Tile Glider simulation directly inside the modal.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Every component is modular and preconfigurable—from solver parameters and factory layouts to chemical libraries and recipe orders.

9
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Now entering Tile Glider—the dedicated high-fidelity simulator for full-scale trajectory telemetry.

10
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,500
Launching our newest simulation run to inspect live multi-mover trajectory execution.

11
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Spring-physics animations ensure centered, realistic mover dynamics across normal, fast, and high-speed presets.

12
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,500
The interactive frame scrubber provides instant timeline seeking with accumulated 50-shade thermal traffic heatmaps.

13
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,500
Collisions are strictly accounted for in the scheduler: up to three movers can safely share and navigate the same tile simultaneously without any collision risk, shown simply as a badge to reduce visual clutter.

14
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,500
Complete end-to-end control from experiment configuration to visual telemetry.

